# ------------------------------------------- v3.76 patch36: one name, one voice
# The owner's identity ledger, 797 blocks: every line left through the sample
# its request asked for - and three NPC lines were NAMED after the player on
# the way, teaching the cache that Maxxor speaks maleyoungeager. The patch40
# rule (a player name never attaches to another voicetype) guarded only the
# queue rung; the pin, the run and the Meta pick each walked past it. The rule
# now has one spelling and every rung asks it. And the state read stops paying
# 0.7 s per poll for two silent ports: a down verdict holds between clicks,
# and a launch click busts the whole cache so the next read asks the world.
section("v3.76 patch36: one name, one voice")

