# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.76 patch90
section("v3.76 patch90: the two late blocks join the card properly")
# Speculative Decoding and Draftless speculation were the only sections that
# would not fold, and the owner read the cause off the symptom: they are written
# by hand at the end of the card rather than produced by the group loop, so they
# never got the heading that folds. They use the same heading now, so whatever
# is added to it reaches all of them. And the fold is keyed by CARD as well as
# group - the cards are compared side by side, and a fold that followed the
# group everywhere made that impossible.
check("function pgrpKey(sid, g)" in JS
      and 'return String(sid) + "\u0001" + String(g);' in JS,
      "the fold is remembered per card AND per group")
check("function pgrpShut(sid, g)" in JS and "function pgrpHead(sid, g, extra)" in JS,
      "and every reader is given both")
