# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.76 patch94
section("v3.76 patch94: the rule that kept being wrong is gone")
# Three patches were spent deciding when the report may stop asking: by state
# name (p92 - "loading" and "down" are states too), by sameness (p88 - a slow
# load pauses), by readiness (p93 - ready is written in the same sweep as the
# last buffers). Each was defensible; each left a card frozen half-read. Every
# one was a guess about when a log has finished being written, which is not
# knowable from outside. So there is no rule now.
_ot94 = seg(JS, "function vramOwnTick", "function vramTick")
check("state.slots.forEach(function (s) {" in _ot94,
      "the tick asks for every slot, every time")
nin(JS, "vramSettled",
    "and no settle state survives - it is the thing that kept wedging")
nin(_ot94, "r.ready", "nothing about readiness is consulted")
nin(_ot94, "slotBusy", "nor about whether a press is in flight")
check("which is not knowable from the outside" in JS
      and "a rule that must be right about timing" in JS,
      "with the three failed rules named, so nobody rebuilds one")
check("less than the page already spends on its own" in JS,
      "and the cost stated, because doing it unconditionally is only right if "
      "it is cheap")
